## Bounded Q13/Q14 search report

Search terms included combinations of:

- rank-one binary matrix recovery from row/column sums or margins;
- rectangle indicator recovery from marginals;
- low-rank Boolean/GF(2) matrices with conditioned marginals;
- parity relation matrices and rectangle decompositions;
- real rank, nonnegative rank, binary-factor rank, GF(2) rank, Boolean/OR rank.

The search did locate standard rank-one row/column-margin recovery discussions and broad low-rank/binary-factorization literature, but **did not locate the exact fixed-cut identifiability-depth statement**
\[
\kappa(C_1)=\max(p,q),\qquad \kappa(C_r)=p+q\quad(r\ge2)
\]
under the project's labeled conditioned-count operator. This is reported only as a bounded-search result. **Exact firstness remains unresolved.**

## Rank-notation boundary

For Q13/Q14 the following five notions are kept distinct even though the same threshold proof happens to work at ranks 1 and 2:

1. ordinary real rank;
2. nonnegative rank;
3. binary-factor rank under standard arithmetic;
4. GF(2) rank;
5. Boolean-OR rank.

“Ordinary rank of a sign matrix” is **not** communication-complexity **sign-rank**. Likewise, every threshold statement here is for one declared fixed cut/order. It is not an all-variable-order separation for OBDDs, tensor networks, or communication protocols.
